WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.120 --> 00:00:06.120
The toughest decision in politics is zoning issues.

2
00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:11.140
Any time you have a zoning issue you’ve got a whole group of people over here that want it,

3
00:00:11.140 --> 00:00:14.960
and a whole group of people over here that don’t want it.

4
00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:18.820
I kin it to being like a basketball official.

5
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:26.580
When a basketball official blows a whistle, usually fifty percent this team’s not going to like it, and this team is, and that team’s not.

6
00:00:26.580 --> 00:00:31.940
So it’s almost like whenever you’re doing a zoning case, you’re going to have people at odds.

7
00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:36.480
Those are the toughest and I take them the most serious, but . . . yeah.

8
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.960
What about rezoning Mossville into heavy industrial?

9
00:00:39.960 --> 00:00:40.700
Tough.

10
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:40.980
Tough.

11
00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:41.800
What was that like?

12
00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:43.280
Yeah that’s tough decisions.

13
00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:54.980
Because you see the factors of what Sasol’s going to bring with this economic development, but you also see people that’s lived there all their life.

14
00:00:54.980 --> 00:01:00.260
But in my opinion, Sasol was more than fair.

15
00:01:00.260 --> 00:01:11.160
The people that they . . . needed their property for a project was paid very well.

16
00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:14.780
The people that they just wanted to be a good neighbor and say,

17
00:01:14.780 --> 00:01:22.300
“Hey we’re going to give you an opportunity to sell on the VPP [voluntary property purchase] plan and buyout sixty percent above appraised value.”

18
00:01:22.300 --> 00:01:27.440
Plus paying closing costs, plus incentives if you signed early and stuff like this.

19
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:33.700
You offer me sixty percent above appraised value of my house right now, you can have the clothes.

20
00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:35.920
I’ll just go.

21
00:01:35.920 --> 00:01:37.960
That’s a tremendous offer.

22
00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:43.560
In fact, I think it’s even better than . . . We all remember the history of Love Canal.

23
00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:47.100
That was a better offer than what the people got at Love Canal.

24
00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:52.140
So I feel like Sasol’s been very fair in their offer.

25
00:01:52.140 --> 00:02:02.880
I feel like there are some people in Mossville have been very unfair in wanting to stay and try to get more.

26
00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:05.300
And that’s a tough situation.

27
00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:09.800
Some people want to stay because they want to stay . . . They don’t want to leave their home site.

28
00:02:09.800 --> 00:02:13.160
But there are some people that want to stay because they’re holding out.

29
00:02:13.160 --> 00:02:15.340
And I think those people are going to lose in the long run.

30
00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:18.880
They should have took the very fair offer from the beginning.

31
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:20.080
My opinion.

32
00:02:20.080 --> 00:02:24.580
But you can point-counterpoint that all day.

33
00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:33.760
But my opinion is Sasol, as an industry with they’ve done, has been very fair to the majority of the people.

34
00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:39.680
There’s some people that didn’t want to leave, and it hurts them to leave, and it’s their community and their history.

35
00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:52.320
But for the better good of the entire Calcasieu Parish and everything, we can’t let an eleven billion dollar project not come to southwest Louisiana.

36
00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:54.000
Is there growing pains?

37
00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.540
Absolutely.

38
00:02:55.540 --> 00:02:59.020
Is there people that having to leave their home that didn’t want to leave their home?

39
00:02:59.020 --> 00:02:59.340
Yes.

40
00:02:59.340 --> 00:03:03.600
Is there people that are waiting in traffic much longer or at the restaurant much longer?

41
00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:04.280
We all are.

42
00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.820
But it’s going to be better in the long run for all of us and I’m excited about that.
